        "orario": "19:51",
        "timestamp": 1774378261,
        "contenuto_esteso": "Advertisement Crime World Americas Judge allows Brazil’s Bolsonaro to serve 27-year sentence at home due to ill health The former president, jailed in November for a coup attempt, was recently in intensive care because of kidney problems and other issues 1 -MIN READ 1 -MIN Listen Associated Press Published: 2:51am, 25 Mar 2026 Brazil’s former president Jair Bolsonaro received permission on Tuesday from a top Brazilian justice to serve his 27-year sentence for a coup attempt at home instead of in prison because of his failing health. The decision by Supreme Court Justice Alexandre de Moraes followed Bolsonaro’s hospitalisation since March 13 for pneumonia , one of several health problems the former leader has faced since he was stabbed by a man in 2018 before he was elected president. Bolsonaro recently was in intensive care for a few days because of kidney problems and other issues. His doctors did not say when he would leave the hospital in Brasilia but his overall condition has improved. Advertisement The family of the right-wing leader had been requesting that the court send him home since he was convicted in November. Bolsonaro was transferred from the local federal police headquarters to a larger cell in January. On Monday Paulo Gonet, Brazil’s attorney general, paved the way for Bolsonaro to be put under house arrest instead of returning to prison. Advertisement Bolsonaro governed between 2019 and 2022. One of his sons, Senator Flavio Bolsonaro, has said he will run for the presidency in October. Polls show he is in a dead heat with incumbent Luiz Inacio Lula da Silva . Advertisement Select Voice Select Speed 00:00 00:00 1.00"
